      "content": "It's understandable that you want all possible support and might be considering ways to feel more focused during finals week. However, \"stacking\" stimulants by combining prescribed medication, like Ritalin, with additional caffeine or energy drinks carries significant risks, even if you feel healthy. This can lead to increased side effects, potential interactions between substances, and even adverse health consequences. Modifying your prescribed medication without professional guidance can be dangerous. It’s crucial to prioritize safety and communicate with your healthcare provider about your needs during this high-pressure time to explore safe and effective strategies together. Remember, your health and well-being are important, and finding sustainable study practices in consultation with your doctor is the best course of action.",
